Patch 3007: the tick-locked audio's output keeps a cushion, rate-controls it, conceals its gaps and counts them (AUDIO_LOCK_SMOOTH=0 turns it off).

Symptom (testers, 2-player rollback): choppy audio. In the tick-locked mode (patch 3005) the 6-7 blocks of a tick reach the device in one
burst at the tick boundary, with no reserve in the 60 ms WASAPI buffer: a late tick (a rollback re-run, a flip schedule restart, the
time-sync stretch, frame jitter) ran the device dry (a hard cut), and once dry it stayed at its floor; a burst into a fuller buffer dropped
whole blocks. Revision 1 (test3) kept a 17 ms cushion in the 60 ms buffer: the test3 testers still had 31 and 53 gaps and 68 and 109
dropped blocks in one 3.2 min match.

Revision 2, for the OUTPUT only (blocks mixed, read index and notify events are exactly as in 3005, so determinism is untouched; the mix
thread never waits on the device in the lock):
- the device opens with AUDIO_LOCK_BUF_MS (default 150; 0 = as before) when that is more than PS3_AUDIO_BUF_MS (60); the free-running mode
  still fills only PS3_AUDIO_BUF_MS of it, so menus and offline keep their latency;
- a cushion of AUDIO_LOCK_CUSHION_MS (default 50) kept by rate control: the smoothed level before each burst steers a continuous linear
  resampler by up to AUDIO_LOCK_DRC/256 (default 4 = 1.6%);
- a block that does not fit is time-compressed into the room left; only under half a block of room is it dropped (both counted);
- when the device falls under AUDIO_LOCK_LOW_MS (default 12) between ticks, the last 15 ms played are looped with crossfaded seams and a
  decaying gain (silence after AUDIO_LOCK_CONCEAL_MS, default 150) instead of running dry, and the next real block crossfades in;
- one "[audio-lock]" line when the lock ends (device underruns, concealed gaps, squeezed / dropped blocks, rate range, level), every ~5 s
  with AUDIO_LOCK_LOG=1, also with the smoothing off.

